cff-version: 1.2.0
title: Colorblind Me
message: >-
  If you use this software or its method, please cite it, and please also cite
  the work it reimplements — the simulation model and the prior art on
  personalised simulation listed under references.
type: software
authors:
  - name: The Colorblind Me contributors
abstract: >-
  Measures where an individual's colour discrimination actually breaks down,
  fits the Machado (2009) severity parameter to that measurement, and encodes
  the result as a short code carried in a URL fragment, so a colour-blind
  person can show someone else what they actually see rather than the
  worst-case dichromacy every off-the-shelf simulator displays.
keywords:
  - colour vision deficiency
  - colour blindness
  - accessibility
  - psychophysics
  - simulation
license: Apache-2.0
references:
  - type: article
    title: >-
      A Physiologically-based Model for Simulation of Color Vision Deficiency
    authors:
      - family-names: Machado
        given-names: Gustavo M.
      - family-names: Oliveira
        given-names: Manuel M.
      - family-names: Fernandes
        given-names: Leandro A. F.
    journal: IEEE Transactions on Visualization and Computer Graphics
    volume: 15
    issue: 6
    start: 1291
    end: 1298
    year: 2009
    doi: 10.1109/TVCG.2009.113
    notes: >-
      Source of the severity-parameterised matrices. Note the published typo in
      equations 17 and 18, page 1295; this project uses the pre-computed
      matrices and so is unaffected.
  - type: conference-paper
    title: >-
      Individual models of color differentiation to improve interpretability of
      information visualization
    authors:
      - family-names: Flatla
        given-names: David R.
      - family-names: Gutwin
        given-names: Carl
    collection-title: >-
      Proceedings of the SIGCHI Conference on Human Factors in Computing Systems
    year: 2010
    doi: 10.1145/1753326.1753715
  - type: conference-paper
    title: >-
      "So that's what you see": building understanding with personalized
      simulations of colour vision deficiency
    authors:
      - family-names: Flatla
        given-names: David R.
      - family-names: Gutwin
        given-names: Carl
    collection-title: >-
      Proceedings of the 14th International ACM SIGACCESS Conference on
      Computers and Accessibility
    year: 2012
    notes: >-
      The idea this project applies. DOI not yet confirmed against the ACM
      record; see docs/prior-art.md.
  - type: conference-paper
    title: Real-Time Mobile Personalized Simulations of Impaired Colour Vision
    authors:
      - family-names: McAlpine
        given-names: R.
      - family-names: Flatla
        given-names: David R.
    collection-title: >-
      Proceedings of the 18th International ACM SIGACCESS Conference on
      Computers and Accessibility
    start: 181
    end: 189
    year: 2016
    doi: 10.1145/2982142.2982170
    notes: >-
      Author surname appears as both McAlpine and MacAlpine across sources, and
      author order varies; confirm against the ACM record before quoting.
  - type: software
    title: Colour
    authors:
      - name: Colour Developers
    repository-code: https://github.com/colour-science/colour
    license: BSD-3-Clause
    notes: >-
      Source of the pre-computed CVD_MATRICES_MACHADO2010 dataset embedded in
      src/core/machado.js. See NOTICE.
